  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the departure of Gibran Rakabuming Raka from the vice presidency after a two-year tenure, the Indonesian political landscape has shifted toward the selection of a successor. The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) has scheduled the formal election for December 2 and has organized a 36-member committee to oversee the verification of potential candidates. President Prabowo Subianto has directed coalition members to submit two names for consideration within the next seven days, noting that candidates are not strictly required to be members of established coalition parties. Various political factions, including the National Mandate Party (PAN), are currently evaluating their stance, with some advocating for candidates capable of addressing national economic challenges. The selection process remains a primary focus of parliamentary activity as the administration moves to fill the vacant leadership position swiftly.",
